  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 46. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 今夜 — 今日の夜。\n2. コース — 進む道筋や決まった順路。\n3. コーティング — 表面を薄い膜などで覆うこと。\n4. コード — 電気製品などにつなぐ被覆された電線。\n5. コーナー — 物の角やある目的のために分けた一角。\n6. コーヒーカップ — コーヒーを飲むためのカップ。\n7. コーラス — 複数の人が声を合わせて歌うこと。\n8. コーンスターチ — トウモロコシから取ったでんぷん。\n9. 合格 — 試験などで定められた基準を満たすこと。\n10. 合計 — いくつかの数を全部足した数。\n11. 合成 — 複数のものを合わせて新しいものを作ること。\n12. 合同 — いくつかの団体などがいっしょに行うこと。\n13. 合流 — 川や道などが一つにつながること。\n14. 号令 — 人がそろって動くために出す声の合図。\n15. 語学 — 外国語などの言葉を学ぶこと。\n16. 午前中 — 朝から正午までの間。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\nCRITICAL GEOMETRY: every panel must be an IDENTICAL square, exactly as the provided template. Do not expand any row for its illustration. Horizontal lines at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100% and vertical lines at the same fractions, all five continuous and pure magenta. The third internal horizontal line MUST stay at 75% height.\n",
